LED PWM: ESP32-P4 LEDC controller driver

The ESP32-P4 LEDC block provides 8 PWM channels over 4 timers with a
shared clock selector.  This driver programs the timer divider (Q10.8)
and per-channel duty, leaving pin routing to whatever configured it
(on Tab5 the boot shim routes channel 0 to GPIO22 for the LCD
backlight).  Clock source is fixed to XTAL 40 MHz, which the shim
already selected and Linux never gates.

